          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:#0a0709;font-family:Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1b1013'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;min-height:100%;padding:3.4cqw 5cqw 4cqw;background:linear-gradient(160deg,#efe8da,#e2d8c4 55%,#d2c6ac);border:.5cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.2cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318'>Derry case file · first seen 1986</div><div style='font:700 6.4cqw/1 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1b1013;margin:1.2cqw 0 .6cqw'>Pennywise</div><div style='font:italic 1.9cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#a4161a'>Shapeshifter · predator · trickster</div><section style='margin-top:2.4cqw;padding-top:0cqw;'><div style='width:100%;aspect-ratio:780 / 590;border-radius:1.2cqw;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 .4cqw 1.2cqw rgba(42,33,24,.35)'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 780 590' width='100%' height='100%' preserveAspectRatio='xMidYMid meet' role='img' aria-label='Pennywise the Clown character dossier'><defs><linearGradient id='case' x1='0' y1='0' x2='1' y2='1'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#1d1215'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#0c0709'/></linearGradient><radialGradient id='glow' cx='50%' cy='96%' r='80%'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#b3141f'/><stop offset='.5' stop-color='#3a0a10'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#080607'/></radialGradient><radialGradient id='balloon' cx='35%' cy='30%' r='75%'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#ff6b6b'/><stop offset='.5' stop-color='#c1121f'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#6e0b13'/></radialGradient><clipPath id='drain'><circle cx='209' cy='294' r='156'/></clipPath></defs><rect width='780' height='590' rx='14' fill='url(#case)'/><rect x='15' y='15' width='750' height='560' rx='6' fill='none' stroke='#7d1318' stroke-width='2'/><path d='M36 104H744M36 481H744' stroke='#7d1318' stroke-width='2'/><text x='38' y='47' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='14' letter-spacing='4' fill='#e5a9ad'>DERRY, MAINE · CASE FILE</text><text x='742' y='47' font-family='monospace' font-size='13' text-anchor='end' fill='#e5a9ad'>EVERY 27 YEARS</text><text x='390' y='92' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='51' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#f4efe6'>PENNYWISE</text><g clip-path='url(#drain)'><rect x='53' y='138' width='312' height='312' fill='url(#glow)'/><rect x='53' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='79' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='105' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='131' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='157' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='183' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='209' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='235' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='261' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='287' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='313' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='339' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><rect x='365' y='138' width='7' height='312' fill='#05080a' opacity='.55'/><path d='M96 452Q104 394 160 382L258 382Q314 394 322 452Z' fill='#8c97a0' stroke='#2a2f33' stroke-width='4'/><circle cx='209' cy='412' r='8' fill='#e8742a'/><circle cx='209' cy='436' r='8' fill='#e8742a'/><circle cx='152' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='167' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='182' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='197' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='212' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='227' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='242' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='257' cy='376' r='16' fill='#e9e4d8' stroke='#4a4a4a' stroke-width='2'/><path d='M162 242Q156 148 208 128Q260 148 254 242Q252 330 208 354Q166 330 162 242Z' fill='#f1ece1' stroke='#2a2023' stroke-width='3'/><path d='M165 192Q128 172 124 216Q150 226 169 212Z' fill='#b4471c' stroke='#5a210c' stroke-width='2'/><path d='M251 192Q288 172 292 216Q266 226 247 212Z' fill='#b4471c' stroke='#5a210c' stroke-width='2'/><path d='M172 216Q187 203 204 213M214 213Q231 203 246 216' fill='none' stroke='#2a2023' stroke-width='3.2' stroke-linecap='round'/><ellipse cx='187' cy='238' rx='14' ry='9' fill='#e9d88a' stroke='#2a2023' stroke-width='2'/><ellipse cx='231' cy='237' rx='14' ry='9' fill='#e9d88a' stroke='#2a2023' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='190' cy='239' r='3.4' fill='#120a0a'/><circle cx='226' cy='235' r='3.4' fill='#120a0a'/><path d='M190 250Q185 292 196 314M226 250Q231 292 220 314' fill='none' stroke='#c1121f' stroke-width='4.2' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M208 262Q215 277 204 281' fill='none' stroke='#b8a99a' stroke-width='2.4' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M174 304Q208 346 242 304Q208 322 174 304Z' fill='#a30f19' stroke='#4d070c' stroke-width='2.4'/><path d='M312 250Q300 300 318 340' fill='none' stroke='#cfcfcf' stroke-width='1.6'/><ellipse cx='316' cy='212' rx='24' ry='29' fill='url(#balloon)'/><path d='M311 240L316 247L321 240Z' fill='#8e0f19'/></g><circle cx='209' cy='294' r='156' fill='none' stroke='#6b6f73' stroke-width='14'/><circle cx='209' cy='294' r='149' fill='none' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='2'/><circle cx='372.0' cy='294.0' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='355.9' cy='364.7' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='310.6' cy='421.4' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='245.3' cy='452.9' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='172.7' cy='452.9' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='107.4' cy='421.4' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='62.1' cy='364.7' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='46.0' cy='294.0' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='62.1' cy='223.3' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='107.4' cy='166.6' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='172.7' cy='135.1' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='245.3' cy='135.1' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='310.6' cy='166.6' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><circle cx='355.9' cy='223.3' r='4.4' fill='#80868a' stroke='#2b2f32' stroke-width='1.2'/><text x='209' y='486' text-anchor='middle' font-family='monospace' font-size='11' fill='#e5a9ad' letter-spacing='2'>FROM THE DRAIN / ARTIST RENDERING</text><g font-family='monospace' font-size='14' fill='#e63946'><text x='406' y='158'>KNOWN AS</text><text x='406' y='225'>REAL NATURE</text><text x='406' y='291'>SPECIALTIES</text><text x='406' y='390'>DISTINGUISHING FEATURES</text></g><g font-family='Georgia,serif' fill='#f4ecec'><text x='406' y='186' font-size='23'>Pennywise, \"Bob\" Gray</text><text x='406' y='252' font-size='23'>It: a thing older than Derry</text><text x='406' y='319' font-size='21'>Fear · shapeshifting</text><text x='406' y='346' font-size='21'>Patience · tricks</text><text x='406' y='420' font-size='20'>Silver suit · orange pompoms</text><text x='406' y='449' font-size='20'>A red balloon, always</text></g><path d='M407 198H735M407 265H735M407 361H735' stroke='#7d1318'/><text x='390' y='520' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='28' font-style='italic' text-anchor='middle' fill='#f4efe6'>It only looks like a clown</text><text x='390' y='552' font-family='monospace' font-size='12' letter-spacing='3' text-anchor='middle' fill='#e5a9ad'>SHAPESHIFTER · PREDATOR · TRICKSTER</text></svg></div></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>01 · Character Profile</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>The Thing in the Storm Drain</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Known as:</b> Pennywise the Dancing Clown, also &quot;Bob&quot; Gray</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Real nature:</b> It, a shapeshifting being far older than the town it hunts</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Home:</b> Derry, Maine</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Creator:</b> Stephen King</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>First appearance:</b> <i>It</i> (1986)</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>On screen:</b> Tim Curry (1990), Bill Skarsgård (2017 and 2019)</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Cycle:</b> Wakes about every 27 years to feed</p><hr style='border:0;border-top:.15cqw solid #c1121f;margin:1.6cqw 0;opacity:.7'><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>Personality</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Playful, cruel, patient and always hungry.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>The clown is a costume. What lives under it feeds on fear, and prefers its meals young.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>It smiles first and attacks later, because a frightened victim is the whole point.</p></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>02 · Unsettling Abilities</div><div style='width:100%;aspect-ratio:490 / 430;border-radius:1.2cqw;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 .4cqw 1.2cqw rgba(42,33,24,.35)'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 490 430' width='100%' height='100%' preserveAspectRatio='xMidYMid meet' role='img' aria-label='Pennywise unsettling abilities'><rect width='490' height='430' rx='16' fill='#170d10'/><text x='30' y='47' font-family='Georgia,serif' font-size='29' font-weight='bold' fill='#f4efe6'>UNSETTLING ABILITIES</text><text x='30' y='72' font-family='monospace' font-size='12' fill='#e5a9ad'>ILLUSTRATIVE RATINGS / 10</text><g font-family='system-ui' font-size='15' fill='#f4ecec'><text x='30' y='111'>SHAPESHIFTING</text><text x='30' y='151'>FEAR READING</text><text x='30' y='191'>PATIENCE</text><text x='30' y='231'>ILLUSION</text><text x='30' y='271'>STRENGTH</text><text x='30' y='311'>CUNNING</text><text x='30' y='351'>MERCY</text><text x='30' y='391'>HONESTY</text></g><g fill='#3a2328'><rect x='204' y='94' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='134' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='174' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='214' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='254' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='294' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='334' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='374' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/></g><g fill='#c1121f'><rect x='204' y='94' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='134' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='174' width='226' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='214' width='203' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='254' width='181' height='14' rx='7'/><rect x='204' y='294' width='181' height='14' rx='7'/></g></svg></div></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>03 · The Costume and Its Props</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>The Costume and Its Props</div><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Suit</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>A baggy silver costume with orange pompoms, and a ruffled collar worn like a joke.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Balloon</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>A red balloon, offered to a child. It is bait, and it is always the same colour.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Voice</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>A friendly, sing-song voice, or any voice that will make a child stop and listen.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Drains</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Storm drains and sewers: the doorways to a lair beneath the whole town.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Deadlights</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Its true gaze: orange lights that drive a person mad if they look into them.</p><hr style='border:0;border-top:.15cqw solid #c1121f;margin:1.6cqw 0;opacity:.7'><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Field philosophy:</b> A friendly face is the cheapest lure there is.</p></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>04 · Strengths and Weaknesses</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>Strengths and Weaknesses</div><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>Strengths</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Shapeshifting:</b> Becomes whatever a person fears most.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Reading fear:</b> Knows what each child dreads, and uses it.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Patience:</b> Sleeps for decades and loses nothing.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Influence over Derry:</b> The town&#39;s adults look away, and It likes it that way.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Age:</b> It has been feeding there for longer than the town has existed.</p><hr style='border:0;border-top:.15cqw solid #c1121f;margin:1.6cqw 0;opacity:.7'><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>Weaknesses</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Courage:</b> A child who stops being afraid takes away its power.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Friendship:</b> A group who trust one another is far harder to frighten than a child alone.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Contempt:</b> It underestimates children, and that is how it can be hurt.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>A body:</b> When it takes a physical form it can be wounded.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Mockery:</b> What it loves to be is dreadful; being laughed at makes it smaller.</p></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>05 · Prey, Rivals and Pawns</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>Prey, Rivals and Pawns</div><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Losers&#39; Club</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>The Seven Who Stand Up to It</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Seven outcasts who face It as children, and come back together as adults to finish the job.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>Bill Denbrough</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Rival / Leader of the Losers</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>A stuttering boy whose grief over his little brother turns into the courage that leads the fight.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>Beverly Marsh</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Rival / The Group&#39;s Fighter</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Quick, fearless and fiercely loyal to the friends who make her braver.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>Henry Bowers</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Unwitting Pawn</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>A cruel bully whom It steers and uses, without a thought for what happens to him.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>Derry</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Home / Accomplice</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>A town that keeps its worst secrets, so the feeding can go on.</p></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>06 · The Feeding Cycles</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>The Feeding Cycles</div><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>1741 | The Settlers Vanish</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Objective:</b> Feed on a new, remote settlement.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Threat:</b> None. No one is left to tell the story.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>1906 | The Ironworks</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Objective:</b> Feed on a crowded town gathering.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Threat:</b> An explosion that Derry soon prefers not to discuss.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>1930 | The Black Spot</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Objective:</b> Turn a town&#39;s hatred into a meal.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Threat:</b> None. The town does the harm itself.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>1957 to 58 | The Summer of the Losers</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Objective:</b> Feed on the town&#39;s children.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Threat:</b> Seven children who refuse to run any more.</p><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>1984 to 85 | The Return</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Objective:</b> Finish what it started.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Threat:</b> The same seven, grown up, with a plan.</p><hr style='border:0;border-top:.15cqw solid #c1121f;margin:1.6cqw 0;opacity:.7'><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Recurring theme:</b> The monster is only half of Derry&#39;s problem. The other half is everyone who looks away.</p></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>07 · Character Psychology</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>The Heart of the Character</div><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>What does it want?</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>To feed, and to be left alone to do it, again and again.</p><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>What does it need?</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Frightened children, and adults who will not look.</p><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>Its central contradiction</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>An ancient cosmic being chooses to appear as a clown.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>It is terrifying because it is playful, and playful because it enjoys the terror.</p><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>Its fatal flaw</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>Contempt. It cannot imagine that children could ever hurt it.</p><div style='font:700 2cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#a4161a'>Its defining quality</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>It is frightening because it is patient.</b></p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>It does not hurry, and it never needs to. It waits for the next time.</p></section><section style='margin-top:3.2cqw;padding-top:2.2cqw;border-top:.2cqw solid #c1121f'><div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;margin-bottom:1cqw'>08 · Character Essence</div><div style='font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:#1b1013'>PENNYWISE</div><div style='font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:#a4161a;letter-spacing:.02em'>The Clown Who Is Only a Mask</div><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Archetype:</b> Monster / Trickster / Predator</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Motivation:</b> Hunger, and the fear that makes a meal worth having.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Greatest strength:</b> Becoming whatever you are most afraid of.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Greatest weakness:</b> Contempt for the people it hunts.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Internal conflict:</b> Appetite against children who have stopped being afraid.</p><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><b style='color:#1b1013'>Arc:</b> A cycle with no growth, ending when the people it feeds on stop being frightened.</p><hr style='border:0;border-top:.15cqw solid #c1121f;margin:1.6cqw 0;opacity:.7'><p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'><i>The clown is only the bait. The fear is the meal.</i></p></section><div style='margin-top:3.6cqw;font:400 1.1cqw/1.4 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7d1318;text-align:center'>9 sections, assembled in reading order</div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Detail: the whole dossier as one document. The Method writes it from the section cards, in reading order, so edit those and not this.",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
