      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Thing in the Storm Drain\n\n**Known as:** Pennywise the Dancing Clown, also \"Bob\" Gray\n\n**Real nature:** It, a shapeshifting being far older than the town it hunts\n\n**Home:** Derry, Maine\n\n**Creator:** Stephen King\n\n**First appearance:** *It* (1986)\n\n**On screen:** Tim Curry (1990), Bill Skarsgård (2017 and 2019)\n\n**Cycle:** Wakes about every 27 years to feed\n\n---\n\n### Personality\n\nPlayful, cruel, patient and always hungry.\n\nThe clown is a costume. What lives under it feeds on fear, and prefers its meals young.\n\nIt smiles first and attacks later, because a frightened victim is the whole point."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "a172891e-0c46-4340-8f33-cbc257b6bd7e"
