      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#1a1013",
        "color": "#f1e8e8",
        "borderColor": "#e9c46a",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Strengths and Weaknesses\n\n## Strengths\n\n**Shapeshifting:** Becomes whatever a person fears most.\n\n**Reading fear:** Knows what each child dreads, and uses it.\n\n**Patience:** Sleeps for decades and loses nothing.\n\n**Influence over Derry:** The town's adults look away, and It likes it that way.\n\n**Age:** It has been feeding there for longer than the town has existed.\n\n---\n\n## Weaknesses\n\n**Courage:** A child who stops being afraid takes away its power.\n\n**Friendship:** A group who trust one another is far harder to frighten than a child alone.\n\n**Contempt:** It underestimates children, and that is how it can be hurt.\n\n**A body:** When it takes a physical form it can be wounded.\n\n**Mockery:** What it loves to be is dreadful; being laughed at makes it smaller."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "a172891e-0c46-4340-8f33-cbc257b6bd7e"
        },
        "documentOrder": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6814d082-e3c6-41c0-8e63-2824785d1c43",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Prey, Rivals and Pawns",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": -55
      },
      "width": 490,
