      "style": {
        "background": "#1a1013",
        "color": "#f1e8e8",
        "borderColor": "#c1121f",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Feeding Cycles\n\n### 1741 | The Settlers Vanish\n**Objective:** Feed on a new, remote settlement.\n\n**Threat:** None. No one is left to tell the story.\n\n### 1906 | The Ironworks\n**Objective:** Feed on a crowded town gathering.\n\n**Threat:** An explosion that Derry soon prefers not to discuss.\n\n### 1930 | The Black Spot\n**Objective:** Turn a town's hatred into a meal.\n\n**Threat:** None. The town does the harm itself.\n\n### 1957 to 58 | The Summer of the Losers\n**Objective:** Feed on the town's children.\n\n**Threat:** Seven children who refuse to run any more.\n\n### 1984 to 85 | The Return\n**Objective:** Finish what it started.\n\n**Threat:** The same seven, grown up, with a plan.\n\n---\n\n**Recurring theme:** The monster is only half of Derry's problem. The other half is everyone who looks away."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "a172891e-0c46-4340-8f33-cbc257b6bd7e"
        },
        "documentOrder": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "94565d3c-b2d1-4651-a4a3-ecd6df288126",
