      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#1a1013",
        "color": "#f1e8e8",
        "borderColor": "#c1121f",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Heart of the Character\n\n## What does it want?\n\nTo feed, and to be left alone to do it, again and again.\n\n## What does it need?\n\nFrightened children, and adults who will not look.\n\n## Its central contradiction\n\nAn ancient cosmic being chooses to appear as a clown.\n\nIt is terrifying because it is playful, and playful because it enjoys the terror.\n\n## Its fatal flaw\n\nContempt. It cannot imagine that children could ever hurt it.\n\n## Its defining quality\n\n**It is frightening because it is patient.**\n\nIt does not hurry, and it never needs to. It waits for the next time."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "a172891e-0c46-4340-8f33-cbc257b6bd7e"
        },
        "documentOrder": 7
      }
    },
