      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#2a0f14",
        "color": "#fff0f0",
        "borderColor": "#e63946",
        "borderWidth": 3,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "altText": "Vintage expedition dossier featuring Indiana Jones's silhouette, fedora and whip, with his name, profession, era, and defining quotation.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# PENNYWISE\n\n### The Clown Who Is Only a Mask\n\n**Archetype:** Monster / Trickster / Predator\n\n**Motivation:** Hunger, and the fear that makes a meal worth having.\n\n**Greatest strength:** Becoming whatever you are most afraid of.\n\n**Greatest weakness:** Contempt for the people it hunts.\n\n**Internal conflict:** Appetite against children who have stopped being afraid.\n\n**Arc:** A cycle with no growth, ending when the people it feeds on stop being frightened.\n\n---\n\n*The clown is only the bait. The fear is the meal.*"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "a172891e-0c46-4340-8f33-cbc257b6bd7e"
        },
        "documentOrder": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "pennywise-assemble-method",
      "type": "method",
      "label": "Assemble the case file",
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": -955
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 200,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180,
          "portId": "call"
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0,
          "portId": "result"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "scriptName": "Assemble the case file",
        "parameters": [],
        "source": "// Assembles a character dossier from its section cards: nothing is typed into the Detail, the Summary or the Glyph.\r\n// It reads every content card that has a `documentOrder` number, in that order (not by where a card sits on the canvas, so the cards can be rearranged without reordering the document), turns each into\r\n// a section of one page, and writes the Detail (the whole dossier as a document), the Summary (a character card) and the Glyph (its mark). It writes only those three, which its declared effects say.\r\n// How it looks is the root's `dossier` setting: { eyebrow, tagline, role, stamp: { field }, palette, mark, glyph }, so the same Method serves any character.\r\nconst clean = (value) => String(value ?? '').trim();\r\nconst esc = (value) => clean(value).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');\r\nconst SERIF = 'Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif'; const MONO = 'ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace';\r\n\r\nconst nodes = await api.getNodes();\r\nconst root = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'root');\r\nconst cfg = root?.data?.dossier || {};\r\nconst P = { ink: '#2a2118', headline: '#6b4a22', accent: '#b99152', accentDeep: '#8a6a3a', paper: ['#ecdcb0', '#d8c08a', '#c8ae78'], outer: '#1c1712', cardBg: ['#322a1f', '#1a1511'], cardName: '#f3ddb1', cardText: '#f3e7ce', cardSub: '#c9b48a', ...(cfg.palette || {}) };\r\nconst INK = P.ink; const GOLD = P.accent;\r\nconst name = clean(root?.data?.identity?.name) || 'Dossier';\r\nconst sections = nodes\r\n  .filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'content' && Number.isFinite(Number(node.data?.documentOrder)) && node.data?.content)\r\n  .sort((a, b) => Number(a.data.documentOrder) - Number(b.data.documentOrder));\r\n\r\n// A small markdown: headings, bold, italic, rules, lists and paragraphs, which is all the dossier uses.\r\nconst inline = (text) => esc(text).replace(/\\*\\*(.+?)\\*\\*/g, `<b style='color:${INK}'>$1</b>`).replace(/\\*(.+?)\\*/g, '<i>$1</i>');\r\nconst markdown = (source) => {\r\n  const out = []; let paragraph = []; let list = [];\r\n  const flush = () => {\r\n    if (paragraph.length) out.push(`<p style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>${inline(paragraph.join(' '))}</p>`);\r\n    if (list.length) out.push(`<ul style='margin:0 0 1.1cqw;padding-left:2.4cqw;font-size:1.5cqw;line-height:1.55'>${list.map((item) => `<li>${inline(item)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>`);\r\n    paragraph = []; list = [];\r\n  };\r\n  for (const raw of clean(source).split('\\n')) {\r\n    const line = raw.trim();\r\n    if (!line) { flush(); continue; }\r\n    if (/^---+$/.test(line)) { flush(); out.push(`<hr style='border:0;border-top:.15cqw solid ${GOLD};margin:1.6cqw 0;opacity:.7'>`); continue; }\r\n    const heading = /^(#{1,3}) +(.*)$/.exec(line);\r\n    if (heading) {\r\n      flush();\r\n      const level = heading[1].length;\r\n      const style = level === 1 ? `font:700 2.9cqw/1.15 ${SERIF};margin:0 0 1.4cqw;color:${INK}` : level === 2 ? `font:700 2cqw/1.2 ${SERIF};margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:${P.headline}` : `font:700 1.6cqw/1.25 ${SERIF};margin:1.3cqw 0 .4cqw;color:${P.headline};letter-spacing:.02em`;\r\n      out.push(`<div style='${style}'>${inline(heading[2])}</div>`);\r\n      continue;\r\n    }\r\n    if (/^[-*] +/.test(line)) { if (paragraph.length) flush(); list.push(line.replace(/^[-*] +/, '')); continue; }\r\n    paragraph.push(line);\r\n  }\r\n  flush();\r\n  return out.join('');\r\n};\r\n\r\n// An SVG section is drawn as the picture it is, at the page's width, in the shape its own viewBox gives it.\r\nconst picture = (svg) => {\r\n  const box = /viewBox=['\"][-\\d.]+ [-\\d.]+ ([\\d.]+) ([\\d.]+)['\"]/.exec(svg);\r\n  const ratio = box ? `${box[1]} / ${box[2]}` : '4 / 3';\r\n  return `<div style='width:100%;aspect-ratio:${ratio};border-radius:1.2cqw;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 .4cqw 1.2cqw rgba(42,33,24,.35)'>${svg}</div>`;\r\n};\r\n\r\nconst body = sections.map((node, index) => {\r\n  const content = node.data.content;\r\n  const inner = clean(content.kind).toLowerCase() === 'svg' ? picture(String(content.value || '')) : markdown(content.value);\r\n  const label = clean(node.label).split('|').pop().trim();\r\n  const number = String(index).padStart(2, '0');\r\n  return `<section style='margin-top:${index === 0 ? '2.4' : '3.2'}cqw;padding-top:${index === 0 ? '0' : '2.2'}cqw;${index === 0 ? '' : `border-top:.2cqw solid ${GOLD}`}'>`\r\n    + (index === 0 ? '' : `<div style='font:700 1.1cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${P.accentDeep};margin-bottom:1cqw'>${number} · ${esc(label)}</div>`)\r\n    + inner + '</section>';\r\n}).join('');\r\n\r\nconst profile = clean(sections.find((node) => /Profile/i.test(clean(node.label)))?.data?.content?.value);\r\nconst field = (pattern) => (new RegExp(`\\\\*\\\\*${pattern}:\\\\*\\\\*\\\\s*(.+)`).exec(profile) || [])[1] || '';\r\nconst role = clean(cfg.role) || clean(field('Profession')) || clean(field('Occupation')) || 'Character';\r\nconst year = (/\\d{4}/.exec(field(clean(cfg.stamp?.field) || 'Born')) || [''])[0];\r\nconst eyebrow = clean(cfg.eyebrow) || 'Character file';\r\nconst tagline = clean(cfg.tagline) || role;\r\nconst stampText = year ? `${cfg.stamp?.label ? clean(cfg.stamp.label) : 'first seen'} ${year}` : '';\r\n\r\nconst detail = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:${P.outer};font-family:${SERIF};color:${INK}'>`\r\n  + `<div style='box-sizing:border-box;min-height:100%;padding:3.4cqw 5cqw 4cqw;background:linear-gradient(160deg,${P.paper[0]},${P.paper[1]} 55%,${P.paper[2]});border:.5cqw solid ${GOLD}'>`\r\n  + `<div style='font:700 1.2cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${P.accentDeep}'>${esc(eyebrow)}${stampText ? ` · ${esc(stampText)}` : ''}</div>`\r\n  + `<div style='font:700 6.4cqw/1 ${SERIF};letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${INK};margin:1.2cqw 0 .6cqw'>${esc(name)}</div>`\r\n  + `<div style='font:italic 1.9cqw/1.3 ${SERIF};color:${P.headline}'>${esc(tagline)}</div>`\r\n  + body\r\n  + `<div style='margin-top:3.6cqw;font:400 1.1cqw/1.4 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${P.accentDeep};text-align:center'>${sections.length} sections, assembled in reading order</div>`\r\n  + `</div></div>`;\r\n\r\nconst mark = clean(cfg.mark) || '';\r\nconst summary = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'>`\r\n  + `<div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:6cqw 7cqw;border-radius:6cqw;background:linear-gradient(135deg,${P.cardBg[0]},${P.cardBg[1]});border:.9cqw solid ${GOLD};display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6cqw;color:${P.cardText};overflow:hidden'>`\r\n  + (mark ? `<div style='flex:0 0 34cqw'>${mark}</div>` : '')\r\n  + `<div style='min-width:0;flex:1'>`\r\n  + `<div style='font:700 3.2cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${GOLD}'>${esc(eyebrow)}</div>`\r\n  + `<div style='font:700 11cqw/1.02 ${SERIF};letter-spacing:.01em;margin:2.4cqw 0 1.6cqw;color:${P.cardName}'>${esc(name)}</div>`\r\n  + `<div style='font:italic 4.6cqw/1.3 ${SERIF};color:${P.cardSub}'>${esc(role)}</div>`\r\n  + `<div style='margin-top:3cqw;font:600 3.2cqw/1 ${MONO};letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${GOLD}'>${sections.length} sections${year ? ` · ${esc(year)}` : ''}</div>`\r\n  + `</div></div></div>`;\r\n\r\nconst faces = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'face');\r\nconst faceFor = (level) => faces.find((node) => clean(node.data?.semanticLevel) === level);\r\nconst glyph = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'glyph');\r\nfor (const [level, html] of [['detail', detail], ['summary', summary]]) {\r\n  const face = faceFor(level);\r\n  if (face) await api.updateView(face.id, { content: { kind: 'html', value: html } });\r\n}\r\nif (glyph) await api.updateNode(glyph.id, { data: { ...glyph.data, glyph: { kind: 'symbol', value: clean(cfg.glyph?.value) || clean(name).charAt(0).toUpperCase(), color: clean(cfg.glyph?.color) || GOLD } } });\r\nreturn { sections: sections.length };\r\n",
        "effects": [
          {
            "kind": "update-node",
            "targets": [
              "pennywise-detail",
              "pennywise-summary",
              "pennywise-glyph"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "allowMutations": true,
        "dryRun": false,
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "a172891e-0c46-4340-8f33-cbc257b6bd7e"
        },
        "memo": "Reads every content card that has a documentOrder, in that order, and writes the Detail, the Summary and the Glyph. Its look is the root's dossier setting. It runs whenever the graph changes."
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "id": "port-surface",
      "type": "surface",
      "source": "pennywise",
      "target": "pennywise-detail",
      "label": "",
